Patch T3 oracles (rung 1b, task T3's review; gate G5, amendment 24):
protect the platform contract's conformance suite.

- crates/eng-platform-api/src/conformance.rs and
  crates/eng-platform-api/src/conformance/** (the suite: `check`,
  `check_scripted`, the probe app and its scripts) and
  crates/eng-platform-headless/tests/conformance.rs (the suite on
  headless, and the deliberately broken platforms that show each rule
  still bites) join protected.toml and .github/CODEOWNERS. T3's reviewer's
  reason: T11 may be tempted to relax a rule when winit misbehaves, and
  whether a rule may change should be the owner's call. T10 relaxed none
  (its amendment 38 describes two rules the suite cannot see on a
  desktop, for the owner).
- No xtask step: `tests` runs both harnesses.

Base: main with T10's commit and t10-oracles.patch applied. Apply both in
one command, best before T11:
  git apply docs/rungs/1b/patches/t10-oracles.patch \
            docs/rungs/1b/patches/t3-oracles.patch
then `cargo xtask quick` and `CI=1 cargo xtask ci --job lint` (docs-check
wants the CODEOWNERS lines). t8-oracles.patch goes on top, after T11.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

